# Overworld (Over)
1. Player controller.(@158455972579552109)
	1. Player's movement will be largely constrained to the horizontal plane.(@16470098290579551538)
	2. Controlled largely thru keyboard.(@4057359145727073018)
	3. Player will have their stamina, hp, and affinities exposed to the overworld.(@13977967063554720592)
		1. All stats should have the ability to regenerate overtime, with the exact rate being adjustable.(@11167689440989266699)
	4. Overworld spells.(@13177450868467670674)
		1. Player should have the ability to use certain spells in the overworld.(@3637818524981319528)
		2. Accessing these spells should be straightforward (no deep menus).(@12927390295256370612)
	5. Player's partners should follow them closely.(@5043925264516831302)
		1. If a partner gets stuck, teleport them to the player's position.(@12688312621439297000)
		2. Partners should not obstruct player.(@7180663358581215774)
	6. Level design.(@42657584933772299)
		1. Assets should be modeled and textured in Blender.(@14191188016667340564)
	7. Enemies.(@10399147032650558130)
		1. Enemy spawn frequency and location should be easily controlled.(@3706534993281387204)
		2. Initiate combat on collision or interaction.(@9194058139824915026)
			1. Enemies that require interaction should have the option of before and after dialog.(@4702966547249179627)
# Story (STRY)
1. Use dialog nodes to talk with NPCs.(@8837853166851985954)
	1. A character has simple dialog that remains constant throughout the game.(@691467087424049585)
	2. A character has simple dialog that changes once or twice.(@12862933997141898906)
	3. Multiple characters engage in a conversation with the player.(@6445982508737473354)
	4. A character gives/takes an item to/from the player.(@730164950245924672)
	5. Character gives the player a quest. Dialog changes depending on results/progress.(@8931436819624264488)
	6. Character reacts to an item the player has (e.g. a key item).(@5298548722540192689)
	7. Character is able to remember simple info the player gives them (e.g. a character specific nickname).(@11132630029477523964)
	8. A cutscene plays while one or more characters talk.(@2730108847152573023)
	9. Combat:(@2398179263088893934)
		1. A character talks with the player before starting a battle.(@12871367800829934863)
		2. A character talks with the player during a battle.(@9710274895126798073)
		3. A character talks after a battle has finished.(@902564965187290834)
	2. Player can buy/sell items to a vendor.(@6228681354019003004)
# Character Management and Inventory (CHAR)
1. Pause overworld/battle when this menu is opened.(@16447949750479701312)
2. Give player option to save/exit game.(@12174322752223044051)
3. Allow player to modify settings.(@578027087303066951)
4. View info about player characters.(@197387760772079764)
	1. Screen to view MC, Alice, and Alex's info + any temp partners.(@10634668745361117661)
		2. General info.(@11938761463201998160)
			1. Name(@11195106850211492595)
			2. Primary and Secondary element.(@5444998034631256766)
			3. Elemental Bias(@2558280816673245118)
			4. Level and experience.(@1149146743521957026)
		3. Display animated sprite/model of character currently being viewed.(@9756356396843506701)
	2. Stat management.(@11473409437599797888)
		1. Show base stats.(@5415687545727066122)
		2. Show how stats are being modified, if applicable.(@2733470542011835338)
		3. Allow stats to be modified in debug mode.(@17679180379807419800)
	3. Equip/remove equipment.(@4804118963066337802)
		1. Limit how much equipment can be attached to a character at a time.(@18127634790908161330)
		2. Query inventory for valid equipment to attach to character.(@12652872821058636443)
			1. Allow player to read detailed info about the equipment before and after equipping it.(@5861364596396052258)
			2. Equipment should have 2 levels of filters.(@14559212297581053094)
				1. If a character doesn't meet the requirements, don't show item in list.(@16976986938084529599)
				2. If player meets requirements, but is already at their limit (see `3.1`), show and disable it.(@3589288215679807180)
			3. Upon applying equipment, immediately apply its effects.(@11482307381863060603)
				1. Euqipment should store all data necessary to reverse its effects upon the character equipping it.(@15959058484151824468)
			4. Upon removing equipment, reverse effects.(@6237779845833126592)
		4. Spell management.(@3248804555172222849)
			1. Display spell details.(@5710013486842276837)
			2. Get list of available spells.(@16345988956373284286)
				1. List of SpellScrolls that character meets the requirements for (movepool).(@5268243273224747557)
			3. Remove spell from moveset.(@5544965710708865838)
			4. Replace spell.(@7869153900713469574)
			5. Replace empty moveset slot with spells from movepool.(@5182228041800868221)
			6. Reorder moveset.(@14928667576741106526)
		5. Inventory.(@7817864365443262892)
			1. View info about items.(@7856230649196244783)
			2. Different items should define rules about when/where they can be used.(@9426312741873053630)
				1. Items that can be used in battle will have a BattleItem component.(@13924693303065787547)
				2. Allow game to query inventory for key items during story events.(@14560922414230453954)
				3. Types of requirements:(@5509727560801203866)
					1. Character (Companions/Player).(@5483438266973543349)
					2. Elemental Bias.(@464081646853590996)
						1. Alices Fated Bias.(@13618780343529997842)
					3. Current typing (Primary/secondary agnostic). *This one will need to be updated during the battle.(@1105464550231461004)
					4. Base stats.(@3103930921126828793)
					5. Status conditions. *This one will need to be updated during the battle.(@3786393650796148596)
				3. Allow player to pick up items from the overworld.(@15928085734430041340)
				4. Allow player to obtain items from other characters.(@4523368955866563679)
				5. Remove items when used by player.(@16356235109515567153)
					1. In battle.(@17066447013771777037)
					2. In overworld.(@14464764003333047771)
				6. Allow user to sort inventory.(@9823512311773171999)
					1. Alphabetically.(@5188019596101813835)
					2. By id.(@14502905621924959343)
				7. Allow user to filter items based on certain criteria.(@13088991104452421517)
					1. Quantity (zero quantity is hidden).(@4169943933677324685)
					2. Name.(@17937358270583218116)
					3. Requirements: boolean whether it has a requirement.(@691281841778169235)
						1. Unusable.(@3826752748302788752)
						2. Bias.(@8474329122355900522)
						3. Elemental.(@10098015782861566468)
						4. Character.(@8785193706087189383)
					8. Battle Usage.(@14764491784018602112)
						1. Battle should have direct access to inventory.(@13425031933707986283)
						2. Disable items on a BattleActor basis.(@7843605573165519833)
						3. Allow a player to select an item to use, but don't officially use it until they end their turn.(@1845567632664753131)
							1. Prevent player from double spending an item (e.g. if the player only has 1 item left, currently theres no mechanism to prevent them from selecting it from 2 different actors on the same turn).(@1924737782734647470)
